<h1 class="no-break">ABSTRACT</h1>
<p>
Electoral democracy relies fundamentally on two competing pillars: rigorous verification of voter eligibility (guaranteeing one citizen, one vote) and absolute ballot secrecy (guaranteeing that cast votes can never be traced back to the citizen). Traditional paper balloting and first-generation Electronic Voting Machines (EVMs) struggle with administrative friction, voter roll manipulation, identity impersonation, and costly manual tallying.
</p>
<p>
This project presents <strong>SecureVote</strong>, an enterprise-grade, database-driven biometric voter authentication and anonymous election platform architected on <strong>Oracle Database 21c Express Edition (XE)</strong>. The system couples biometric identity verification with zero-linkage ballot storage. The database schema enforces an unbreachable separation of concerns: the <code>VOTER</code> entity maintains citizen demographics, salted SHA-256 government ID hashes, and AES-256-GCM application-encrypted biometric templates, while the <code>VOTE</code> entity stores strictly anonymized ballot choices stamped solely with calendar dates (DATE) to eliminate side-channel timing correlation attacks. Authentication is mediated via single-use, cryptographically signed JSON Web Tokens (<code>vote_token</code>) tracked in an active token registry (<code>CONSUMED_VOTE_TOKENS</code>) to prevent replay exploits.
</p>
<p>
The software stack integrates Oracle 21c XE (thin-mode connection pooling via <code>python-oracledb</code>), a high-performance <strong>FastAPI</strong> backend supporting PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 operator credentials, and a modern <strong>Next.js 16 (React 19)</strong> kiosk interface featuring glassmorphic controls and hardware bypass simulation for testing environments. Rigorous unit, integration, and security testing demonstrated sub-15ms query execution, mathematical voter deduplication, automated fraud lockout windows, and complete audit trail integrity in <code>VERIFICATION_LOG</code>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Keywords:</strong> Oracle Database 21c, Biometric Authentication, Ballot Anonymity, Data Integrity, Relational Database Normalization, Cryptographic Separation.
</p>

